  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Site Management, GBV services, NFIs,  Wash to IDPs and Returnees for the increased protection of women and girls in Gombi and Hong LGAs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThis project will contribute to the protection of girls and vulnerable women in Gombi and Hong LGA&#x2019;s of Adamawa State through an integrated CCCM, WASH, Shelter/NFI, and protection response. The project will enhance the protective environment of vulnerable communities, especially vulnerable women, and girls.ltbrgtThe innovative approach that is in our multi-sectoral approach which embraces partnerships with local organizations and government agencies. This places a strong emphasis on collaboration between sectors seamlessly integrating protection, WASH, and NFIs. This increases faster access to services as all actors are present in project locations, unlike previous CCCM programming where needs and gaps will be communicated to partners through the sector. Also, through the sub-implementing partner, Big Family 360 will be deploying the smart RR application which provides the GBV survivor with quick access to GBV service at no cost without any form of internet required with the use of their normal phones and a USSD code.ltbrgtThe response will be implemented in Gombi and Hong Local Government Areas of Adamawa state. HARAF will implement the integrated and multisectoral CCCM and Shelter/NFI approach while its implementing partner Big Family 360 will implement the GBV response and SORASUN Foundation will implement the WASH response in all 2 LGAs. Particularly, HARAF will set up appropriate accountability mechanisms (community meetings, toll-free lines, suggestion box) through which affected populations can measure the adequacy of interventions, and address concerns and complaints in each LGA.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
